// D5470 — `is K[]` over a record literal's empty list field nothing stores into, at every delivery
// position and in both faces. An empty list fits every `K[]` (the D4771 ruling), so the test holds
// whatever element the un-annotated face's list defaults to; the HIT reads only the scalar, since a
// narrowed read of the field itself is D4964's.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
// @@VALUE@@
{ n: 1, kids: [] }
// @@TYPE@@
{ n: i32, kids: string[] }
// @@TEST@@
v.kids is string[] && v.n == 1
// @@HIT@@
print(v.n)
// @@MISS@@
print("miss")
// @@WANT@@
1
